---
title: How to Write a Software Engineer Job Description That Attracts the Right Applicants (Template)
publishedAt: 2026-11-11
type: companies
---
**Quick answer:** A good software engineer job description opens with what the person will build and why it matters, then lists three to six real requirements, a short "nice to have" list, the tech stack, the salary range, location or remote policy, and the interview process. Use a clear, searchable title like "Senior Backend Engineer (Go)", write in plain language, and cut anything that's a preference rather than a requirement. Posts that are specific and show pay attract fewer unqualified applicants and more of the people you actually want.

The job description is the first filter in your hiring process. A vague post brings in hundreds of applicants who don't fit and puts off the strong engineers who do, because they can't tell whether the role is worth their time. A clear post does part of your screening for you.

